      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That loud whistling and whining noise primarily comes from high-velocity air rushing through the turbocharger's narrow scroll housing at startup. Additionally, as the turbo spools up quickly, high-pressure air escaping faster than the compressor wheels can move it creates a phenomenon known as whine, which can also be amplified when the drive belt slips briefly. This rapid sound characteristic is caused by changes in airflow dynamics and internal pressure differentials rather than mechanical misalignment.",
